  <!-- WHERE LIO WINS -->
  <section class="lio-lp-vs__wins">
    <div class="lio-lp-vs__wrap">
      <h2>Where Lio wins</h2>
      <div class="lio-lp-vs__wins-list">
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__win">
          <div class="lio-lp-vs__win-num">1</div>
          <div>
            <h3>The only device with handcrafted wood &mdash; every piece unique</h3>
            <p>Capnos is aluminum or plastic. Ripple+ is plastic. MOXĒ is plastic. LUVV is plastic. Cigtrus is disposable plastic. Cloudy is plastic. Lio is olive or walnut wood, hand-finished, with grain variation in every unit. If you&rsquo;re going to hold a device in your hand 50 times a day, it should feel like an object you own &mdash; not like a disposable pen. This isn&rsquo;t a cosmetic detail. Users tell us the physical quality is a big part of why Lio replaces the habit so effectively &mdash; it feels like a ritual object, not a medicinal aid.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__win">
          <div class="lio-lp-vs__win-num">2</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Actually no battery, actually no vapor</h3>
            <p>Read the fine print on Ripple+ and LUVV. Both are electronic devices with batteries that heat a formula and produce inhalable vapor. Both are technically e-cigarettes (just without nicotine). Both are restricted on planes, in many offices, and in most places vapes are banned. Lio, Capnos, Cigtrus, MOXĒ, and Cloudy are all genuinely non-electronic. You can use Lio on a plane. In a meeting. At a restaurant. No one will notice &mdash; there&rsquo;s nothing to exhale.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__win">
          <div class="lio-lp-vs__win-num">3</div>
          <div>
            <h3>The smartest core system in the category</h3>
            <p>Capnos makes you drip essential oils onto a wick inside the device and wait for it to soak. MOXĒ is a single-use pen &mdash; when it&rsquo;s done, you throw it out. Ripple+ and LUVV use proprietary pods that cost ~$15 each. Cigtrus is entirely disposable. Lio&rsquo;s flavor cores are pre-saturated cotton plugs you fray, insert, and use for 2 days &mdash; then swap. No drip, no dry time, no alignment, no battery decoding.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__win">
          <div class="lio-lp-vs__win-num">4</div>
          <div>
            <h3>The only three-tier device lineup</h3>
            <p>Most competitors offer one device, maybe two. Lio offers three: Original (fixed airflow, €29), Plus (adjustable airflow, +€9), and Pro (adjustable airflow + magnetic fidgeting, +€59). Heavy former smokers tend to want tighter airflow resistance &mdash; the Plus. Anxious fidgeters and nail-biters want the extra tactile input of the magnetic fidget &mdash; the Pro. Casual vape-curious users start with Original. Competitors force one-size-fits-all. Lio meets you where your habit actually is.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__win">
          <div class="lio-lp-vs__win-num">5</div>
          <div>
            <h3>150,000+ customers and 1,000+ 5-star reviews</h3>
            <p>Capnos has shipped ~90,000 units globally. Most other competitors don&rsquo;t publish user counts at all. Lio has passed 150,000 users and accumulated over 1,000 verified 5-star reviews. That scale isn&rsquo;t just marketing &mdash; it&rsquo;s a signal that this category has a clear leader, and the wisdom-of-crowds has already chosen.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HONEST SECTION -->
