    <div class="lio-lp-vs__wrap">
      <h2>Where competitors win (we'll be honest)</h2>
      <p class="lio-sub">No product is best at everything. Here&rsquo;s when another option might suit you better.</p>
      <div class="lio-lp-vs__honest-list">
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__honest-item">
          <strong>Capnos</strong>
          <p>If your primary craving is the pressurized "throat hit" &mdash; the pop of a pull &mdash; Capnos&rsquo;s silicone valve delivers a stronger physical pressure than Lio&rsquo;s smooth airflow. For throat-hit purists, this is legitimate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__honest-item">
          <strong>Ripple+</strong>
          <p>If you want a nicotine-free device that looks and feels exactly like a vape &mdash; visible exhale and all &mdash; Ripple+ is closer to the traditional vape experience. But you won&rsquo;t break the vape ritual using it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__honest-item">
          <strong>Cigtrus</strong>
          <p>If you&rsquo;re testing the entire flavored air concept for under $15 before committing, Cigtrus is a reasonable experiment. You&rsquo;ll likely outgrow it in a week.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lio-lp-vs__honest-item">
          <strong>MOXĒ</strong>
          <p>If your habit is mild and you mostly want a pleasant mint/essential-oil inhale a few times a day, MOXĒ is a clean, honest wellness pen.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

